## Launch controls and diagnostic value

The prior repeated-pass native attempt completed all eight pass begin/end pairs; pass 8 ended at cumulative process CPU 21.786911 seconds, then emit reached its 30-second deadline without post-loop markers. The first new `post-reach-begin` marker sits immediately after that loop, and later markers bracket reach, sections, runtime C generation, ID rewriting, and the C file write. One capped run can therefore locate progress beyond the previously observed final-pass boundary. Marker CPU values are cumulative process CPU; adjacent differences are diagnostic only, with synchronous stderr writes adding small perturbation.

The outer plan’s 143 preactivation pins all match. Its SOURCE02 freeze/archive hashes match; all 53 activation inventory entries agree with the frozen inventory, five backup hashes match their preactivation bodies, and the remaining 48 are unchanged. The native plan’s only five preactivation pin differences are those five bodies, which activation replaces before delivery and source-boundary preflights. Generated C/native outputs are absent. The single native command uses CPU 3 and caps of 30/120/5 seconds against the full 207,834-byte oracle (`14565a3635124edb3ba8ef53b76e2030c3b3698e5d7c4a31989bc3ca9fb54a2d`). The outer activation lock differs from the collector’s `/tmp/bendvy-parity-heavy.lock`; its `finally` restores all five bodies and checks all 53 inventory entries.

If emit still reaches its cap, retain the raw markers and incomplete receipt, confirm restoration, and claim no C/build/consumer result. Even a complete consumer pass remains bounded candidate evidence only.
